ceptual architecture for Agentic-AI-powered deployment pipelines that transition from rigid workflows to feedback-driven control loops. The architecture integrates specialized agents such as those for requirement formatting, automated test scenario generation, and real-time monitoring, governed by explicit authority boundaries and \"Decision Package\" escalation policies for human-in-the-loop validation. The proposed framework aims to mitigate cognitive load on engineering teams by delegating routine, low-precision tasks to intelligent agents while preserving strategic human judgment. By bridging established software engineering principles with emerging agentic architectures, this thesis contributes a structured roadmap for the responsible implementation of autonomous decision-making systems in high-velocity delivery environments. Evaluated through a metrics-based comparison grounded in the systematic literature review, the results demonstrate significant improvements in pipeline lead time (~95% reduction), output consistency (3× increase in BDD scenario coverage), shift-left security detection, and 100% completeness when compared to a traditional manual DevOps baseline."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W4413894893", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-7490243/v1", "title": "The Inadequacy of Classical and Quantum Frameworks for Predictive Autonomous Agents in Non-Stationary Environments", "publication_year": 2025, "type": "preprint", "cited_by_count": 0, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-7490243/latest.pdf", "any_repository_has_fulltext": true}, "primary_location": {"id": "doi:10.21203/rs.3.rs-7490243/v1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-7490243/v1", "is_oa": true, "landing_page_url": "https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-7490243/v1", "pdf_url": "https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-7490243/latest.pdf", "source": {"id": "https://openalex.org/S4306525896", "display_name": "Research